75	// are shown oldest first, each as "<user> on <date>: <text>", the date being the sheet's today when it was written.
76	// A DRAFT claim takes lines with the line label, quantity and unit amount and the add-line button; its amount is then the
77	// quantities times the unit amounts added up, and its lines are shown oldest first as "<label> <qty> x <unit>". Adding a line
78	// counts as editing the claim: a claim that is not a DRAFT, in a closed period or locked by another user is refused with
79	// the claim's error, as is a blank label, a quantity that is not a whole number of at least 1, or a unit with more than two decimals.
80	// A DRAFT claim is deleted with the delete button (any other status, or a claim whose due-by is inside a closed period, is
81	// refused with the claim's error): it is DELETED, counts nowhere and cannot be edited, opened or voided. On the same
82	// sheet-today it was deleted the restore button makes it a DRAFT again; on a later day that is refused with the claim's error.
