    27	 * start, then every N days; or the day in every month from the start's month, on the month's last day when it is shorter,
    28	 * dates before the start left out) up to the end and the sheet's today that has none yet, dated that day with an empty note, each
    29	 * audited as CLAIM_ADDED. A date the claim form refuses (its due-by inside a closed period, after the person's retirement) is
    30	 * skipped, and tried again on the next generate. A viewer changes nothing: their generate makes no claim (an archived sheet
    31	 * refuses it). A plan naming a descendant sheet makes its claims there instead, for the person of the same name on that sheet (none
    32	 * when there is no such person), by that sheet's rules and audited on that sheet; they still count towards what the plan made.
